Frame can convert an audio file or export audio from a video source. Choose the output format in **General**, then configure the **Audio** section.

## Choose the tracks

Check the source audio tracks you want to export. Only selected tracks are included. This matters for sources with several languages, commentary tracks, or alternate mixes.

Review track selection after changing the output format. The container determines the supported audio codecs and track combinations.

## Choose an audio format

Audio output formats include MP3, M4A, WAV, FLAC, and Opus. The available encoders also cover AAC, AC-3, ALAC, PCM, and transport-stream audio where supported.

| Goal | Starting point |
| --- | --- |
| Widely supported compressed audio | MP3 or AAC in M4A |
| Preserve a lossless source | FLAC or an appropriate PCM/WAV configuration |
| Compact audio for a compatible destination | Opus |

Converting a lossy source to FLAC or WAV does not restore discarded detail. It changes the output encoding and can increase the file size.

## Bitrate, quality, and channels

Set the bitrate or VBR quality when the chosen encoder supports it. Use the channel layout controls to match the intended output, and adjust volume if needed.

Check the exported file at a normal listening level. Changing channels or gain can alter a mix even when the video is unchanged.

<DocsScreenshot
  scene="audio-output"
