  caption="Choose the audio tracks and encoding settings for the output."
/>

## Audio filters

Frame provides normalization, limiting, compression, bass and treble adjustment, high-pass and low-pass filters, noise reduction, de-essing, and stereo-width controls.

Start with one filter and compare the result. A limiter controls peaks; a compressor changes dynamic range. Heavy noise reduction or compression can introduce audible artifacts.

<DocsScreenshot
  scene="audio-filters"
  alt="Frame Output inspector showing audio filter controls."
  caption="Audio filters provide adjustments for levels, dynamics, and tone."
/>

## Reuse an audio setup

Use **Audio MP3** or **Audio FLAC (Lossless)** in the Presets tab, or save a custom preset after configuring the output. See [presets](/docs/presets) and [batch conversion](/docs/batch-conversion).
